note P-103
  from: explorations/coordinator/positions-audit/full/evidence/corrections-c8.md, "History lines for the entries kept word for word"; by: the POSITIONS audit, chunk c8 (its writer's history lines, in the noted form), at his word of 2026-10-22 08:19 UTC, which approved the audit as a run; note: the text is kept word for word; this block gives the curator's messages behind it, by their times: the note that `d39d6fe75` wrote with these times was lost when `a88e52bf7` rebuilt the histories, and this block puts them back. Its sources: 2026-09-29T18:52:49.920Z, he asks what a suite is for if it cannot simply be run to green, and says that the values that matter must be part of the test, answering the coordinator's 2026-09-29T18:07:00.343Z offer to take the "before" outputs once per base and share them among the rungs. 2026-09-29T19:03:33.775Z, the suite does not care what a test prints beyond its checks, because it does not matter, answering the coordinator's 2026-09-29T19:01:59.766Z (the 18 tests that print differently are the team's own). 2026-10-02T15:48:05.965Z, it was decided in the post-mortem: the suite's original design has its own mechanism for the values that matter, a test that passes needs no control of its outputs, and the offer is not to be raised again, answering the coordinator's 2026-10-02T15:40:56.635Z offer of expected-output files.

